description:
Write a module `bank` whose `Account` keeps its balance private, so the only way to change it is through methods that keep it valid:

```rust
mod bank {
    #[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]
    pub enum BankError { InvalidAmount, InsufficientFunds { needed: u64, available: u64 }, SameAccount }

    pub struct Account { /* private: id, owner, balance in cents */ }

    impl Account {
        pub fn open(id: u32, owner: &str) -> Account
        pub fn id(&self) -> u32
        pub fn owner(&self) -> &str
        pub fn balance(&self) -> u64
        pub fn deposit(&mut self, cents: u64) -> Result<(), BankError>           // 0 is InvalidAmount
        pub fn withdraw(&mut self, cents: u64) -> Result<(), BankError>          // InsufficientFunds when short
    }

    pub fn transfer(from: &mut Account, to: &mut Account, cents: u64) -> Result<(), BankError>   // nothing changes on error

    pub mod report {
        pub fn summary(accounts: &[super::Account]) -> String   // "3 accounts, total 12.34"
    }
}
```

- `transfer` between accounts with the same id fails with `SameAccount`; an amount of 0 with `InvalidAmount`.
- `summary` writes the total in euros with 2 decimals.

